 "_about": "Built-in stdcall argument counts for common Win32 APIs, for the emulator's stand-in of an import (emulate/emulator.py _builtin_argc) when the exporting module's code does not say (symbols/api_arguments.py). Public, documented ABI facts (the number of dword arguments each takes) -- not inferences about the binary -- so the environment can clean the stack correctly for the frequent cases with no SDK configured. Extend as real targets surface more. wsprintf-family (cdecl/variadic) are intentionally absent (cdecl cleanup is 0, the default). Keyed by bare name; A/W variants share a count.",
